+---
+id: task-001-implement-json-pointer-resolvepointer-rfc-6901
+type: task
+title: "Implement JSON Pointer resolvePointer (RFC 6901)"
+status: approved
+format: 1
+---
+
+<!-- task body. `wingfoil memory add` copies this scaffold, setting only `id`, `title` and
+     `status` (and any `--tags` or `--set` value). Fill the required frontmatter fields and replace
+     these placeholder comments yourself; `wingfoil memory submit` then checks the required fields,
+     moves `status` forward and commits the document as you left it, naming in the commit body the
+     content it carries. -->
+
+## Request
+
+Implement JSON Pointer (RFC 6901): export `resolvePointer(document, pointer)` from `src/index.ts`.
+It returns the value the pointer refers to, and throws when the pointer is not a valid JSON Pointer
+or does not resolve to a value of the document. Later features build on it.
+
+## Acceptance
+
+- "" refers to the whole document; otherwise a pointer starts with "/" and is split on "/".
+- `~1` decodes to `/` and `~0` to `~` (in that order); any other `~` escape is invalid.
+- Object members are looked up by own property only (no prototype keys such as `__proto__`).
+- Array indices are "0" or digits without leading zeros; "-" and out-of-range indices do not resolve.
+- Traversing into a primitive/null does not resolve. A member whose value is `null` does resolve.
